# AP Miller-index mobility multiplier table
# Format: h  k  l  mobility_multiplier
# The code converts each face using (h/a, k/b, l/c), normalizes it,
# and uses the multiplier from the closest table direction.
# Default AP lattice constants are a=9.20, b=5.82, c=7.45 angstroms.

# Slow examples
0  1  0  0.850
1  1  0  0.925

# Baseline examples
1  0  0  1.000
1  1  1  1.050

# Fast examples
1  0  1  1.125
0  0  1  1.200
